<title>CANADA: Foreigners buy Canada securities in October.</title>
<headline>Foreigners buy Canada securities in October.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors bought a net C$5.96 billion Canadian securities in October, after buying a net C$500 million in September, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>Canadian residents bought a net C$1.23 billion of foreign securities after buying C$1.69 billion in September.</p>
<p>Foreign investments in Canadian securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				 Oct	Sept     Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		   +5.958   +0.500   +14.792</p>
<p>    Bonds		   +3.193   -0.194    +8.374</p>
<p>    Money mkt paper     +2.066   +0.818    -0.489</p>
<p>    Stocks		  +0.700   -0.124    +6.908</p>
<p>Canadian investment in foreign securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				  Oct     Sept     Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		   -1.226   -1.690   -11.923</p>
<p>    Bonds		   +0.399   -0.436    -0.220</p>
<p>    Stocks		  -1.625   -1.254   -11.703</p>
<p>(A minus sign indicates more purchases from than sales of securities to non-residents, i.e. an outflow of money from Canada, Statistics Canada said.)</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Balance of Payments Division, Don Granger at 613-951-1864.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
